# S05: Stock Ledger, Recipes and Prep-Batch Waste

> *«Есть товар. Есть его остаток. Есть расход. Есть поставщик. Есть закупка. И есть момент,
> когда товара становится слишком мало…»*
>
> *«Щеглов вечером выливает остатки соусов и моет чаны.»* — the vat is this sprint's prep batch.

## Objective

Replace the read-only percentage fixture with a real stock ledger. Connect menu items to
ingredients through recipes that include **per-modifier lines**, so the sauce is consumed only
when the sauce is chosen. Post consumption from a Postgres trigger so a sale and its depletion
cannot diverge. Add prep batches so end-of-shift remainders become visible waste rather than an
invisible margin leak.

## What "inventory" means today

`server/api/inventory.get.ts` is 24 lines: `import orders from '~/fixtures/orders.json'` then
`return orders.inventory`. No Supabase, no auth, no role guard. Shape:
`{id:'ing-1', name:'Tequila', amount:'750ml', remaining:60, unit:'%'}` — `remaining` is a
**percentage** and `unit` is the literal string `'%'` on all 27 rows. The real unit of measure is
trapped in the `amount` string and recovered by regex at `InventoryItemCard.vue:166-170`, which
breaks on `'5 dozen'` and `'24 bottles'`.

A grep for `inventory|stock|ingredient|supplier|recipe|reorder|purchase` across all 24 migrations
returns **zero** matches. Nothing decrements on sale, across all four write paths.

