## The packaging decision

The article's *«количество упаковочного материала на единицу заказа»* is cheap to model now — a
`packaging` department on `stock_items` plus a recipe line on every food item — and expensive to
backfill later, because there is no historical consumption data to reconstruct from. **Decided
here, in T01/T03, not deferred.**

## Definition of Done

- [ ] Serving a dish deducts its ingredients, its chosen sauce **and** its packaging, inside the
      database, exactly once even under a replayed update
- [ ] Declining or refunding a served line restores the exact quantities
- [ ] A scripted 50-order simulation ends with `stock_balances` equal to the signed sum of
      `stock_movements` for every item
- [ ] Closing a prep batch records the remainder as waste attributable to a shift
- [ ] Reorder suggestions name a supplier, a lead time and a projected run-out date **in the venue
      timezone**
- [ ] `fixtures/orders.json` inventory is read by no code; the fixture endpoint is deleted
- [ ] An out-of-stock dish renders **sold out** instead of silently vanishing from the menu
- [ ] **Owner-visible deliverable:** end-of-shift remainder capture — the sauce-vat surface

## Invariants Produced

1. Stock changes only by inserting a `stock_movements` row. No code may update
   `quantity_on_hand` directly.
2. Consumption is posted by `post_stock_consumption()` inside the database, never by
   application-side sequencing. (supabase-js has no transaction primitive; the existing
   compensating-delete pattern already leaks — `orders.post.ts:151-192` rolls back the order but
   the `table_assignments` insert survives.)
3. Every stock movement carries an `idempotency_key` and a `source_type`/`source_id` pair.
4. A `recipe_line` with `modifier_id` set is consumed only when that modifier is present on the
   order line.
5. Packaging is a first-class stock department; every food item consumes it.
6. Menu sellability is derived from `compute_menu_item_coverage()`. `menu_items.is_available` is
   an operator override only.
7. Recipe edits create a new version; recipe history is immutable.
8. Migration numbering continues at **047**.
